---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Grokati, operated by XenMedia Marketing Limited."
>
  <section class="about-content">
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle muted">Last updated: 14 August 2026</p>

    <p>
      Grokati (<a href="https://grokati.com">grokati.com</a>) is a trading name of
      <strong>XenMedia Marketing Limited</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”). This Privacy Policy explains
      how we handle information when you visit the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      XenMedia Marketing Limited<br />
      Ste 2, 4 Blenheim Court, Peppercorn Close<br />
      Peterborough, PE1 2DU<br />
      United Kingdom<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk">info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk</a>
    </p>

    <h2>What this site does</h2>
    <p>
      Grokati is a static news website that publishes articles about Grok and xAI. Content is
      stored as Markdown files and served as static pages. There is no user account system and no
      comment system on the site in Phase 1.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to collect as little personal data as possible.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Server / hosting logs</strong> — Our hosting provider (Vercel) may automatically
        process standard technical data such as IP address, browser type, and request timestamps
        for security, performance, and abuse prevention.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email</strong> — If you contact us at
        <a href="mailto:info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk">info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk</a>, we will
        process the information you choose to send so we can respond.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not run our own analytics trackers or advertising cookies on the site.
The site does not currently use non-essential cookies that require consent under UK PECR.
Third-party infrastructure (for example the host or font provider) may process limited
technical data under their own policies. Any strictly necessary technical processing required
to deliver the site securely is treated as necessary for the service.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use technical and contact information only to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Operate and secure the website</li>
      <li>Respond to enquiries you send us</li>
      <li>Meet legal obligations if required</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Legal basis</h2>
    <p>
      Where UK GDPR applies, we rely on legitimate interests (running a secure public website) and,
      for email correspondence, on steps taken at your request or our legitimate interest in
      responding to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell personal data. We may share limited technical data with service providers who
      help us host or operate the site (such as Vercel), who process it on our behalf or as
      independent controllers under their own terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Server logs are retained according to our host’s standard practices. Email correspondence is
      kept only as long as needed to handle the enquiry and for reasonable business records.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      If UK data protection law applies to you, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or
      restrict certain personal data, and to object to certain processing. To exercise these rights,
      contact us at
      <a href="mailto:info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk">info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) in the UK.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will change
      when we do.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:
      <a href="mailto:info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk">info@xenmediamarketing.co.uk</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>